# Jmix Fetch Plans Rules

## Scope
Applies to data loading operations

## Built-in Plans
- `_base` — all local attributes
- `_instance_name` — only display name
- `_local` — same as _base

## XML Definition (fetch-plans.xml)
```xml
<fetch-plan entity="Order" name="order-with-lines" extends="_base">
    <property name="customer" fetchPlan="_instance_name"/>
    <property name="lines" fetchPlan="_base"/>
</fetch-plan>
```

## Programmatic
```java
dataManager.load(Order.class)
    .id(id)
    .fetchPlan("order-with-lines")
    .one();
```

## Inline Builder
```java
.fetchPlan(fp -> fp
    .addAll("field1", "field2")
    .add("relation", r -> r.addFetchPlan("_base"))
)
```

## View XML
```xml
<instance id="orderDc" class="Order">
    <fetchPlan extends="_base">
        <property name="customer" fetchPlan="_instance_name"/>
    </fetchPlan>
</instance>
```

## Best Practices
- List views: `_instance_name` for references
- Detail views: `_base` or custom
- Check logs for N+1 queries
